From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: gadget: park packets that slip into the RxFIFO of an idle OUT endpoint

All OUT endpoints share one RxFIFO. In descriptor DMA the core does not set
NAK on a non-isochronous OUT endpoint when its last queued transfer
completes, and NAK set from the completion interrupt comes too late for a
host that keeps sending: its next packets are accepted into the RxFIFO
while the endpoint has no buffer, and every other OUT endpoint of the
gadget waits behind them until the function queues a request for this
one. A USB serial port whose reader stops (closed, or throttled by a slow
reader) while the host writes does that every time; on an SG2002
(DWC_otg 4.20a) 12 of 12 tries left the USB network receiving nothing.
DCFG bit 13 (EnDevOutNak) does not help on this core, and buffer DMA, where
the core does set NAK, costs 8 times the interrupts with UAC1 audio.

So when such an endpoint runs out of requests, set NAK on it, and a timer
tick later look at the RxFIFO head (GRXSTSR, a peek). A packet of this
endpoint there is moved by DMA, one packet per descriptor and with NAK
still set (nothing new comes in), into a 2 KiB buffer of the endpoint (the
RxFIFO cannot hold more). The parked packets go first into the endpoint's
next request: copied after the request is unmapped, the rest of the
transfer by DMA behind them; a request they fill completes from the timer,
not inside the function's usb_ep_queue(). Disconnect, reset and disable
drop them with the endpoint's requests.

The status of a stuck packet read here as PktSts 0xa as well as 2 (bit 20
set), so only the low three bits are compared.

Measured on the SG2002 with a Windows host: the same race 4 of 4 tries
without a stuck RxFIFO; a 16 MiB transfer to the serial port whose reader
was stopped for 2, 6 or 10 s, 7 of 7 runs with equal MD5 on both sides and
every ping over the USB network answered during the stop (about 300
packets parked per run); keyboard, LED reports, 500 mouse reports a second
and UAC1 capture without overruns; with audio and mouse load 1,039 USB
interrupts a second and 4.3-4.5 % of the C906, as without this patch.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core.h b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core.h
index 767251aa1..a6ad2860f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core.h
@@ -156,6 +156,18 @@ struct dwc2_hsotg_ep {
 	unsigned int		next_desc;
 	unsigned int		compl_desc;
 
+	/*
+	 * Descriptor DMA, non-isochronous OUT: packets taken out of the
+	 * RxFIFO while the endpoint had no request (see gadget.c, "park").
+	 */
+	struct timer_list	park_timer;
+	u8			*park_buf;
+	dma_addr_t		park_dma;
+	u16			park_pkt[8];
+	unsigned int		park_cnt;
+	unsigned int		park_tries;
+	unsigned int		parking:1;
+
 	char                    name[10];
 };
 
@@ -169,6 +181,8 @@ struct dwc2_hsotg_req {
 	struct usb_request      req;
 	struct list_head        queue;
 	void *saved_req_buf;
+	unsigned int		park_take;
+	unsigned int		park_serve:1;
 };
 
